														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-997968">
									

<p>… notice how that's so much <em>shorter</em>? We don't need the name of the original deceased, or his date of death (aside from year), or the fact that his gravestone and the cemetery records agreed…</p>
<p>We examined the corpse, so the exhumation is a given. How the SCP was removed from the corpse - who cares? That it wasn't embalmed - how is that relevant?</p>
<p>The fact that other coffins were being drawn towards the SCP - that's useful. What happened to the cemetery after we learned that - we don't care.</p>
<p>See?</p>
<p>Oh, and it really bugs me when our exclusion zones have <em>no margin of safety</em>.</p>
<p>This thing's influence reaches over twelve meters? Then the exclusion zone should be at least <strong>fifteen</strong> meters.</p>

							</div>

								
					
